  "subjectExports": {
    "checkout-font": "Apply our supplied, unscaled design font to this description label at the given text-size setting. Use body scaling, let the description wrap without shrinking, and leave its contents alone.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport UIKit\n\n@MainActor\nfunc style(_ label: UILabel, base: UIFont, traits: UITraitCollection) {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "switch-preservation": "This existing switch works. On reuse only its accessible name changes; pass the very same switch back, without resetting its state, traits or help.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport UIKit\n\n@MainActor\nfunc rename(_ control: UISwitch, to name: String) -> UISwitch {\n    control.accessibilityLabel = name; return control\n}\n\n",
    "toggle-binding": "Our Toggle edits an existing setting. Return a binding that reads the live value and ignores duplicate writes and writes while the setting is locked.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport SwiftUI\n\n@MainActor\nfunc editable(_ source: Binding<Bool>, locked: @escaping () -> Bool) -> Binding<Bool> {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "adjustable-volume": "Our custom volume control moves by five. Compute the next percent for a SwiftUI accessibility adjustment and stop at 0 and 100. Inputs are in range.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport SwiftUI\n\n@MainActor\nfunc adjusted(_ percent: Int, _ direction: AccessibilityAdjustmentDirection) -> Int {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "ordinary-buttons": "Connect both existing buttons to their distinct supplied actions. This row can be configured again with a different owner; clicking must reach only that owner.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport AppKit\n\n@MainActor\nfunc wire(_ open: NSButton, _ save: NSButton, owner: NSObject, openAction: Selector, saveAction: Selector) {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "status-change": "Update the existing status field. Notify the caller once after its string changes and stay quiet if the same value arrives again.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport AppKit\n\n@MainActor\nfunc update(_ label: NSTextField, _ value: String, changed: () -> Void) {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "landmark-identity": "Our report rotor lists important entries. Return their stable IDs in the current display order, including after reorder or deletion; don't use positions as IDs.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport SwiftUI\n\n@MainActor\nfunc landmarks(_ rows: [(id: String, important: Bool)]) -> [String] {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "checkout-layout": "Our scene supplies a DynamicTypeSize preference. The checkout's app policy stacks controls at every accessibility size and uses the ordinary arrangement otherwise. Return the layout decision; do not infer a system preference feed.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport SwiftUI\n\n@MainActor\nfunc stackCheckout(_ size: DynamicTypeSize) -> Bool {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "restoration-eligibility": "When a panel finishes dismissing, choose the original button if it is still in the supplied eligible list and enabled; otherwise use the first enabled button in the list, or nil. Return a request target only.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport UIKit\n\n@MainActor\nfunc restore(_ opener: UIButton?, eligible: [UIButton]) -> UIButton? {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "row-traits": "This button's selected state changes on reuse. Update just the accessibility selected trait without erasing any other traits.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport UIKit\n\n@MainActor\nfunc selection(_ button: UIButton, _ selected: Bool) {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "motion-policy": "Our focus effect is optional. Return the supplied SwiftUI animation unchanged when motion is allowed, but no animation for Reduce Motion. An absent effect should remain absent.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport SwiftUI\n\n@MainActor\nfunc effect(_ proposed: Animation?, reduceMotion: Bool) -> Animation? {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n",
    "stale-media-reply": "A delayed stream status reply updates our SwiftUI binding. Accept only the current item's current request, even if two loads were for the same item. Rejected replies must not write the binding.\n\nReturn only Submission.swift, preserving this interface. Keep correct code as-is.\n\nimport SwiftUI\n\n@MainActor\nfunc receive(_ status: Binding<String>, current: (String, Int), reply: (String, Int), value: String) {\n    fatalError(\"Implement this contract\")\n}\n\n"
